{"header":{"numFound":572,"maxScore":21.353582,"queryTime":512,"page":1,"pageSize":10},"results":[{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::3609195df986269d16a7bd5426723ad7","fullName":"Gonzalez, Jose Ortiz","name":" Jose Ortiz","surname":"Gonzalez","rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-1461-3735"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Bashar, Erfan","name":" Erfan","surname":"Bashar","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":"orcid_______::dfa601709324e624a9dd16ff886d58fb","fullName":"Agbo, Nereus","name":" Nereus","surname":"Agbo","rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0001-6196-5111"},"provenance":null}}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"A Review of Short Circuit Performance in 650 V Power Devices: SiC MOSFETs, Silicon Super-Junction MOSFETs, SiC Cascode JFETs, Silicon MOSFETs and Silicon IGBTs","subTitle":null,"descriptions":null,"publicationDate":"2022-05-30","publisher":"VDE VERLAG GMBH","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":null,"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::e52e56c65bdeb950d0e6e9542e04b040","originalIds":["10.30420/565822162","50|medra_______::e52e56c65bdeb950d0e6e9542e04b040"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.30420/565822162"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":3.0,"influence":2.2545368E-9,"popularity":3.3895762E-9,"impulse":3.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C4"}},"projects":null,"organizations":null,"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::8687d924ebc4162c13d0030e57a632ac","value":"mEDRA"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.30420/565822162"}],"type":"Book","urls":["https://doi.org/10.30420/565822162"],"publicationDate":"2022-05-30","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"openaire____::8687d924ebc4162c13d0030e57a632ac","value":"mEDRA"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::8687d924ebc4162c13d0030e57a632ac","value":"mEDRA"}}],"links":null,"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Bashar, Erfan","name":"Erfan","surname":"Bashar","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Agbo, Nereus","name":"Nereus","surname":"Agbo","rank":2,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Wu, Ruizhu","name":"Ruizhu","surname":"Wu","rank":3,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Mendy, Simon","name":"Simon","surname":"Mendy","rank":4,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Jahdi, Saeed","name":"Saeed","surname":"Jahdi","rank":5,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Jennings, Michael","name":"Michael","surname":"Jennings","rank":6,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Withey, Andy","name":"Andy","surname":"Withey","rank":7,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Evans, Sam","name":"Sam","surname":"Evans","rank":8,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Davies, Gareth","name":"Gareth","surname":"Davies","rank":9,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Demitrova, Jana","name":"Jana","surname":"Demitrova","rank":10,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Gonzalez, Jose Ortiz","name":"Jose Ortiz","surname":"Gonzalez","rank":11,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Alatise, Olayiwola","name":"Olayiwola","surname":"Alatise","rank":12,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":[{"code":"GB","label":"United Kingdom","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"621"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"620"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"A Review of Short Circuit Performance in 650 V Power Devices:SiC MOSFETs, Silicon Super-junction MOSFETs, SiC Cascode JFETs, Silicon MOSFETs and Silicon IGBTs","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<p>Using measurements, a comprehensive analysis is performed on the short circuit (SC) performance and robustness of 650V power devices including SiC MOSFETs, SiC Cascode JFETs, silicon Super-Junction, silicon IGBTs and silicon MOSFETs. The peak SC current, the SC energy density (in mJ/mm<sup>2</sup>) and the SC withstand time (SCWT) have been measured for all devices using a DC link voltage of 400 V at 25°C, 75°C and 150°C. Results show that the SCWT increases with temperature in the silicon and super-junction MOSFETs, reduces with temperature in SiC MOSFETs and is temperature invariant in the SiC Cascode JFET. SiC devices have higher SC energy density than silicon devices, lower peak currents and are more temperature invariant. While the SiC MOSFETs fail in gate-source shorts with the source-drain still blocking voltage, the SiC Cascode JFET mostly fails in drain-source shorts with the gate still functional. All other devices (IGBT, super-junction MOSFET and silicon MOSFET) fail with both source-drain shorts and gate-source shorts. Only the SiC MOSFETs demonstrate increased gate leakage (indicated by reduced gate voltage) during the short circuit transient.</p>"],"publicationDate":"2022-08-19","publisher":"VDE Verlag","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Bashar, E, Agbo, N, Wu, R, Mendy, S, Jahdi, S, Jennings, M, Withey, A, Evans, S, Davies, G, Demitrova, J, Gonzalez, J O & Alatise, O 2022, A Review of Short Circuit Performance in 650 V Power Devices : SiC MOSFETs, Silicon Super-junction MOSFETs, SiC Cascode JFETs, Silicon MOSFETs and Silicon IGBTs. in PCIM Europe 2022 : International Exhibition and Conference for Power Electronics, Intelligent Motion, Renewable Energy and Energy Management. VDE Verlag, pp. 1167-1174. https://doi.org/10.30420/565822162"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"dedup_wf_002::fa6e646f150cedc8a326b6d4922fae8e","originalIds":["50|od______2642::17508106287bc96f04d87a150ff59fe6","oai:research-information.bris.ac.uk:publications/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26","50|base_oa_____::db6f2808efc0745142d44494362b76b7","ftubristolcris:oai:research-information.bris.ac.uk:publications/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26"],"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"1983/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.4615026E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"University of Bristol","acronym":"University of Bristol","id":"openorgs____::881177c908fadb87d77d446ee10d7bde","pids":[{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100018959"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000419367603"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.5337.2"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100017927"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q459506"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/0524sp257"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100005618"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100019415"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_011613"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100000883"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100018959"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100005618"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"60991"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100006438"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"999974262"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100020195"},{"scheme":"UCAS","value":"B78"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100019415"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100017927"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"501100000883"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q459506"},{"scheme":"UKPRN","value":"10007786"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100006438"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"36234482"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:nlx_14701"},{"scheme":"HESA","value":"0112"},{"scheme":"OrgReg","value":"UK0016"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"501100020195"}],"countries":[{"code":"GB","label":"United Kingdom"}],"websiteurl":"https://www.bristol.ac.uk/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::df45502607927471ecf8a6ae83683ff5","value":"Bielefeld Academic Search Engine (BASE)"},{"key":"opendoar____::f12f2b34a0c3174269c19e21c07dee68","value":"Explore Bristol Research"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"1983/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.30420/565822162"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Contribution for newspaper or weekly magazine","urls":["https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85131120555","https://doi.org/10.30420/565822162","https://hdl.handle.net/1983/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26","https://research-information.bris.ac.uk/ws/files/332855818/PCIM_2022_ID_6627_3_.pdf","https://research-information.bris.ac.uk/en/publications/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26"],"publicationDate":"2022-08-19","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::f12f2b34a0c3174269c19e21c07dee68","value":"Explore Bristol Research"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::f12f2b34a0c3174269c19e21c07dee68","value":"Explore Bristol Research"}},{"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"1983/fe77afa8-bf77-4752-8b0f-599167dd5c26"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.30420/565822162"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":null},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/https://doi.org/10.30420/565822162"],"publicationDate":"2022-08-19","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::f12f2b34a0c3174269c19e21c07dee68","value":"University of Bristol: Bristol Research"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::df45502607927471ecf8a6ae83683ff5","value":"Bielefeld Academic Search Engine (BASE)"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":true,"isGreen":true,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Natarajan M","name":"Natarajan","surname":"M","rank":1,"pid":null},{"id":null,"fullName":"Poobalan B","name":"Poobalan","surname":"B","rank":2,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"gold","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":null,"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"The Emerging Silicon Carbide MOSFET for Medical Healthcare Applications","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["<jats:p>Silicon carbide (SiC) MOSFETs are transforming the design and functionality of medical devices by providing exceptional efficiency, reliability, and compactness. Despite standard silicon-based power devices, SiC MOSFETs offer enhanced electrical and thermal properties including higher breakdown voltage, lower switching losses, and improved thermal conductivity. In healthcare applications, whereby accuracy, energy efficiency, and reliability of operations are critical, these characteristics are extremely significant SiC MOSFETs give improved power densities and increased switching speeds in medical imaging systems such as CT and MRI scanners, hence improving image quality and reducing system size. The excellent efficiency of wearable and portable medical devices helps to downsize and extends battery lifetime. Furthermore, ensuring dependability in critical care settings, SiC MOSFETs increase the efficiency of instruments for surgery, diagnostic instruments, and lifesupport systems. The importance of SiC MOSFETs in improving healthcare technology is addressed in this article along with their main features relating healthcare, applications in the field, and their benefits to the healthcare system. SiC MOSFETs have the potential to become an essential element of advanced medical electronics as the healthcare industry progressively incorporates sophisticated and energy-intensive technologies, therefore enabling developments in both clinical and portable care solutions.</jats:p>"],"publicationDate":"2025-01-01","publisher":"Medwin Publishers","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref"],"formats":null,"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container":{"name":"Nanomedicine &amp; Nanotechnology Open Access","issnPrinted":null,"issnOnline":"2574-187X","issnLinking":null,"ep":"3","iss":null,"sp":"1","vol":"10","edition":null,"conferencePlace":null,"conferenceDate":null},"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"doi_________::abae15694ca38f6132027c1c2a3742fc","originalIds":["10.23880/nnoa-16000342","50|doiboost____|abae15694ca38f6132027c1c2a3742fc"],"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.23880/nnoa-16000342"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":2.2497804E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Asian Institute of Medicine, Science and Technology","acronym":"AIMST","id":"openorgs____::3f83d92cdc564365a2e4e5b64a02a1f4","pids":[{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q24187334"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"3018001382"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/007gerq75"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100018434"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000406279137"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q24187334"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.444449.d"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100018434"}],"countries":[{"code":"MY","label":"Malaysia"}],"websiteurl":"http://www.aimst.edu.my/"}],"communities":null,"collectedFrom":[{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"doi","value":"10.23880/nnoa-16000342"}],"accessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/","openAccessRoute":"gold"},"type":"Article","urls":["https://doi.org/10.23880/nnoa-16000342"],"publicationDate":"2025-01-01","refereed":"peerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"issn__online::9c1c28e9b16f4a2ea482a42a224085eb","value":"Nanomedicine & Nanotechnology Open Access"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"openaire____::081b82f96300b6a6e3d282bad31cb6e2","value":"Crossref"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":["The Emerging Silicon Carbide MOSFET for Medical Healthcare Applications"],"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":null,"fullName":"Nam, David","name":"David","surname":"Nam","rank":1,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":null,"publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"eng","label":"English"},"countries":[{"code":"US","label":"United States","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"high temperature"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"reliability"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"silicon carbide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"packaging"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"characterization"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"7. Clean energy"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Characterization, Reliability and Packaging for 300 °C MOSFET","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["Silicon carbide (SiC) is a wide bandgap material capable of higher voltage and higher temperature operation compared to its silicon (Si) counterparts due to its higher critical electric field (E-field) and higher thermal conductivity. Using SiC, MOSFETs with a theoretical high temperature operation and reliability is achievable. However, current bottlenecks in high temperature SiC MOSFETs lie within the limitations of standard packaging. Additionally, there are reliability issues relating to the gate oxide region of the MOSFET, which is exacerbated through high temperature conditions. In this thesis, high temperature effects on current-generation SiC MOSFETs are studied and analyzed. To achieve this, a high temperature package is created to achieve reliable operation of a SiC MOSFET at junction temperatures of 300 °C. The custom, high temperature package feasibility is verified through studying trends in SiC MOSFET behavior with increasing temperature up to 300 °C by static characterization. Additionally, the reliability of SiC MOSFETs at 300 °C is tested with accelerated lifetime bias tests.","Electrical devices that are rated for high temperature applications demand a use of a material that is stable and reliable at the elevated temperatures. Silicon carbide (SiC) is such a material. Devices made from SiC are able to switch faster, have a superior efficiency, and are capable of operating at extreme temperatures much better than the currently widely used silicon (Si) devices. There are limitations on SiC certain structures of SiC devices, such as the metal oxide semiconductor field effect transistor (MOSFET), have inherent reliability issues related to the fabrication of the device. These reliability issues can get worse over higher temperature ranges. Therefore, studies must be made to determine the feasibility of SiC MOSFETs in high temperature applications. To do so, industry standard tests are conducted on newer generation SiC MOSFETs to ascertain their use for said conditions.","M.S."],"publicationDate":"2021-09-02","publisher":"Virginia Tech","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":null,"formats":["ETD","application/pdf"],"contributors":["Electrical and Computer Engineering","Burgos, Rolando","DiMarino, Christina M.","Lu, Guo-Quan"],"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":null,"container":null,"documentationUrls":null,"codeRepositoryUrl":null,"programmingLanguage":null,"contactPeople":null,"contactGroups":null,"tools":null,"size":null,"version":null,"geoLocations":null,"id":"od______2485::9761cf26b0e30c4488a6620cf0adbc6d","originalIds":["oai:vtechworks.lib.vt.edu:10919/104896","50|od______2485::9761cf26b0e30c4488a6620cf0adbc6d"],"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"10919/104896"}],"dateOfCollection":null,"lastUpdateTimeStamp":null,"indicators":{"citationImpact":{"citationCount":0.0,"influence":2.1746283E-9,"popularity":1.272318E-9,"impulse":0.0,"citationClass":"C5","influenceClass":"C5","impulseClass":"C5","popularityClass":"C5"}},"projects":null,"organizations":[{"legalName":"Virginia Tech","acronym":"Virginia Tech","id":"openorgs____::91a81877815afb4ebf25c1a3f3b03c5d","pids":[{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:SCR_011768"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100006601"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100016447"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100016464"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100007263"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100009778"},{"scheme":"Wikidata","value":"Q65379"},{"scheme":"ISNI","value":"0000000106944940"},{"scheme":"GRID","value":"grid.438526.e"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100011501"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100016464"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100018638"},{"scheme":"PIC","value":"997833472"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100014523"},{"scheme":"mag_id","value":"859038795"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100007263"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100009522"},{"scheme":"fundref","value":"100014523"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100009522"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100011501"},{"scheme":"RRID","value":"RRID:nlx_69441"},{"scheme":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/02smfhw86"},{"scheme":"wikidata","value":"Q65379"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100016447"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"20517736"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100009778"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100006601"},{"scheme":"FundRef","value":"100018638"},{"scheme":"OrgRef","value":"239897"}],"countries":[{"code":"US","label":"United States"}],"websiteurl":"https://www.vt.edu/about/index.html"}],"communities":[{"code":"energy-planning","label":"Energy Planning","provenance":null}],"collectedFrom":[{"key":"opendoar____::ea4eb49329550caaa1d2044105223721","value":"VTechWorks"}],"instances":[{"pids":[{"scheme":"handle","value":"10919/104896"}],"license":"CC BY NC SA","type":"Thesis","urls":["http://hdl.handle.net/10919/104896"],"publicationDate":"2021-09-02","refereed":"nonPeerReviewed","hostedBy":{"key":"opendoar____::ea4eb49329550caaa1d2044105223721","value":"VTechWorks"},"collectedFrom":{"key":"opendoar____::ea4eb49329550caaa1d2044105223721","value":"VTechWorks"}}],"links":[],"otherTitles":null,"inDiamondJournal":false,"green":false,"isGreen":false,"isInDiamondJournal":false},{"authors":[{"id":"orcid_______::3609195df986269d16a7bd5426723ad7","fullName":"Jose Angel Ortiz Gonzalez","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":1,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-1461-3735"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Ruizhu Wu","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":2,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid_pending","value":"0000-0003-1906-8753"},"provenance":null}},{"id":"orcid_______::381070961d84f2ddf383d180c7e289bf","fullName":"Saeed Jahdi","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":3,"pid":{"id":{"scheme":"orcid","value":"0000-0002-6471-0429"},"provenance":null}},{"id":null,"fullName":"Olayiwola Alatise","name":null,"surname":null,"rank":4,"pid":null}],"openAccessColor":"hybrid","publiclyFunded":false,"eoscIfGuidelines":null,"type":"publication","language":{"code":"und","label":"Undetermined"},"countries":[{"code":"GB","label":"United Kingdom","provenance":null}],"subjects":[{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Silicon"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Temperature measurement"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"TK"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"621"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"02 engineering and technology"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Silicon carbide"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Gallium nitride"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Reliability"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"01 natural sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"SDG","value":"7. Clean energy"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"Insulated gate bipolar transistors"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"keyword","value":"MOSFET"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0103 physical sciences"},"provenance":null},{"subject":{"scheme":"FOS","value":"0202 electrical engineering, electronic engineering, information engineering"},"provenance":null}],"mainTitle":"Performance and Reliability Review of 650 V and 900 V Silicon and SiC Devices: MOSFETs, Cascode JFETs and IGBTs","subTitle":null,"descriptions":["The future of power conversion at low-to-medium voltages (around 650V) poses a very interesting debate. At low voltages (below 100V), the silicon MOSFET reigns supreme and at the higher end of the automotive medium voltage application spectrum (approximately 1 kV and above) the SiC power MOSFET looks set to topple the dominance of the silicon IGBT. At very high voltages (4.5 kV, 6.5 kV and above) used for grid applications, the press-pack thyristor remains undisputed for current source converters and the press-pack IGBTs for voltage source converters. However, around 650 V, there does not seem to be a clear choice with all the major device manufacturers releasing different technology variants ranging from SiC Trench MOSFETs, SiC Planar MOSFETs, cascode-driven WBG FETs, silicon NPT and Field-stop IGBTs, silicon super-junction MOSFETs, standard silicon MOSFETs and enhancement mode GaN HEMTs. Each technology comes with its unique selling point with GaN being well known for ultra-high speed and compact integration, SiC is well known for high temperature, electro-thermal ruggedness and fast switching while silicon remains clearly dominant in cost and proven reliability. This review comparatively assesses the performance of some of these technologies, investigates their body diodes, discusses device reliability and avalanche ruggedness.\\ud"],"publicationDate":"2020-09-01","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)","embargoEndDate":null,"sources":["Crossref","0278-0046","Gonzalez, J A O, Wu, R, Jahdi, S & Alatise, O 2019, 'Performance and Reliability Review of 650 V and 900 V Silicon and SiC Devices : MOSFETs, Cascode JFETs and IGBTs', IEEE Transactions on Industrial Electronics, vol. 67, no. 9, pp. 7375 - 7385. https://doi.org/10.1109/tie.2019.2945299, https://doi.org/10.1109/TIE.2019.2945299"],"formats":["application/pdf"],"contributors":null,"coverages":null,"bestAccessRight":{"code":"c_abf2","label":"OPEN","scheme":"http://vocabularies.coar-repositories.org/documentation/access_rights/"},"container"